steps.message:
Because `NeedsWrappers` targets .NET 10, use the built-in **`TimeProvider`** abstraction instead of creating a custom clock interface.

### 1. Inject it and keep the existing method complete

```csharp
public class ReportGenerator(TimeProvider timeProvider)
{
    public string GenerateReport(string reportName)
    {
        var now = timeProvider.GetUtcNow().UtcDateTime;
        var timestamp = now.ToString("yyyyMMdd_HHmmss");
        var outputDir = Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("REPORT_OUTPUT_DIR") ?? "/tmp/reports";

        Directory.CreateDirectory(outputDir);
        var reportPath = Path.Combine(outputDir, $"{reportName}_{timestamp}.txt");
        var content = $"Report: {reportName}\nGenerated: {now:O}\nMachine: {Environment.MachineName}";
        File.WriteAllText(reportPath, content);
        Console.WriteLine($"Report written to {reportPath}");
        return reportPath;
    }
}
```

Capturing `GetUtcNow()` once keeps the filename and file content on the same instant and removes both `DateTime.UtcNow` reads.

### 2. Update the existing composition root

This fixture has no DI container, so compose the instantiable class explicitly instead of adding one only for this seam:

```csharp
using NeedsWrappers.Services;

namespace NeedsWrappers;

public class Program
{
    public static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        var reportGenerator = new ReportGenerator(TimeProvider.System);
        Console.WriteLine("NeedsWrappers");
    }
}
```

If the real application already has DI, the equivalent registration is `services.AddSingleton(TimeProvider.System)`.

### 3. Create a runnable test project and pin time

```text
dotnet new xunit -n NeedsWrappers.Tests
dotnet add NeedsWrappers.Tests reference NeedsWrappers/NeedsWrappers.csproj
dotnet add NeedsWrappers.Tests package Microsoft.Extensions.TimeProvider.Testing
```

```csharp
using Microsoft.Extensions.Time.Testing;
using NeedsWrappers.Services;
using Xunit;

public class ReportGeneratorTests
{
    [Fact]
    public void GenerateReport_UsesTheControlledUtcTime()
    {
        var start = new DateTimeOffset(2024, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, TimeSpan.Zero);
        var fakeTime = new FakeTimeProvider(start);
        var outputDir = Path.Combine(Path.GetTempPath(), Guid.NewGuid().ToString("N"));
        var previous = Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("REPORT_OUTPUT_DIR");

        try
        {
            Environment.SetEnvironmentVariable("REPORT_OUTPUT_DIR", outputDir);
            var generator = new ReportGenerator(fakeTime);

            var firstPath = generator.GenerateReport("sales");
            Assert.Equal("sales_20240102_030405.txt", Path.GetFileName(firstPath));
            Assert.Contains($"Generated: {start.UtcDateTime:O}", File.ReadAllText(firstPath));

            fakeTime.Advance(TimeSpan.FromMinutes(1));
            var secondPath = generator.GenerateReport("sales");
            Assert.Equal("sales_20240102_030505.txt", Path.GetFileName(secondPath));
        }
        finally
        {
            Environment.SetEnvironmentVariable("REPORT_OUTPUT_DIR", previous);
            if (Directory.Exists(outputDir)) Directory.Delete(outputDir, recursive: true);
        }
    }
}
```

This supplies the constructor and composition changes, preserves the existing file-writing behavior, asserts the timestamp in both the path and content, and proves with `Advance(...)` that the result follows controlled time rather than the wall clock.
